INT. ASSAY OFFICE - GOLD RUSH TOWN - DAY (1851)

A plank room, one window grimed with dust, a counter scarred by a thousand scales. Weighing pans, crucibles, a brass balance under glass.

THADDEUS WHIT, 50s, spectacles, black sleeve garters, presides behind the counter. His fingers are stained yellow from nitric acid.

The door bangs. CORNELIA BASS, 30s, trousers and a man's hat, strides in. Dust to her knees. A leather pouch swings from her belt.

THADDEUS
We close in ten minutes, madam.

CORNELIA
Then I'll be quick.

She drops the pouch on the counter. It thuds.

THADDEUS
What have you got?

CORNELIA
Color.

He unties the cord. Pours. Dull yellow dust pools on a sheet of paper.

He pinches some. Rolls it between his fingers. Holds it to the light.

THADDEUS
Where was this panned?

CORNELIA
Dry Creek.

THADDEUS
Dry Creek has been dry for a year.

CORNELIA
That's why it's called Dry Creek.

He gives her a thin smile. Reaches for a vial.

THADDEUS
A drop of acid. For the test.

CORNELIA
Go on.

He doses the metal. It stays bright. He nods.

THADDEUS
It's good.

CORNELIA
I know.

THADDEUS
Twelve dollars an ounce.

CORNELIA
Twenty.

THADDEUS
Fourteen.

CORNELIA
Seventeen and the sack.

THADDEUS
Done.

He weighs it. Writes a slip. Counts bills from a strongbox. Slides them over. She doesn't count them.

CORNELIA
You'll be here tomorrow?

THADDEUS
Every day but Sunday.

CORNELIA
Good. I'll bring more.

THADDEUS
Madam, if I may. A woman alone in these hills--

CORNELIA
I'm not alone.

THADDEUS
Your husband?

CORNELIA
My claim. A hundred yards of dirt. And a rifle.

THADDEUS
Ah.

She tips her hat. Heads for the door. Stops with her hand on the latch.

CORNELIA (CONT'D)
Mr. Whit.

THADDEUS
Yes?

CORNELIA
You tested my gold with acid.

THADDEUS
Standard practice.

CORNELIA
And you held it to the light.

THADDEUS
Also standard.

CORNELIA
But you never looked at the weight.

Thaddeus freezes. The pen drops from his fingers.

CORNELIA (CONT'D)
That scale tilts two grains left. I've been watching it for three weeks.

THADDEUS
It's properly calibrated.

CORNELIA
It's not.

THADDEUS
I'll ask you to leave.

CORNELIA
You'll ask me nothing.

She turns back. Her hand slips beneath her coat.

THADDEUS
Madam.

CORNELIA
Open the strongbox.

THADDEUS
This is robbery.

CORNELIA
It's restitution.

He doesn't move. The clock ticks. Dust drifts through the light.

THADDEUS
There's four hundred dollars.

CORNELIA
There's four thousand. Under the false bottom.

Thaddeus goes white. He kneels, trembling, lifts the strongbox's lining.

THADDEUS
How?

CORNELIA
I used to keep books in Sacramento.

He lays a bundle on the counter. Then another. She slides them into her pouch.

CORNELIA (CONT'D)
(over his words)
We never met.

THADDEUS ^
We never met.

They say it together. She smiles. He doesn't.

She leaves. The door clacks shut. The bell above it jingles for a long time.
